---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../../../components/Hero.astro';
import ActivityCard from '../../../components/ActivityCard.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { getRegion, getActivitiesForRegion, REGIONS } from '../../../data/site-data';
import { buildTouristDestinationSchema, buildBreadcrumbSchema } from '../../../data/schema';

const region = getRegion('miami');
const activities = getActivitiesForRegion('miami');

const schema = [
  buildTouristDestinationSchema({
    name: 'Miami',
    description: region.description,
    url: '/florida/miami/',
    activities
  }),
  buildBreadcrumbSchema([
    { label: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { label: 'Florida', url: '/florida/' },
    { label: 'Miami', url: '/florida/miami/' }
  ])
];
---

<Layout title="Miami Water Activities & Tours" description={region.description} schema={schema}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[
    { label: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { label: 'Florida', url: '/florida/' },
    { label: 'Miami' }
  ]} />

  <Hero
    title="Miami Water Activities"
    subtitle="From jet ski rentals on South Beach to snorkeling in Biscayne National Park, Miami is America's water sports capital. Find the best spots, operators, and tours."
  />

  <!-- Activities -->
  <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ocean-900 mb-6">Water Activities in Miami</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      {activities.map(activity => (
        <ActivityCard activitySlug={activity.slug} regionSlug="miami" />
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Sub-destinations -->
  <section class="bg-ocean-50 py-12">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ocean-900 mb-6">Explore Miami by Area</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        {region.subDestinations.map(sub => (
          <a href={`/florida/miami/${sub.slug}/`} class="group bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-ocean-900 group-hover:text-ocean-600">{sub.name}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-2">{sub.description}</p>
            <span class="inline-flex items-center mt-3 text-sm font-medium text-ocean-600">View activities →</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why Miami -->
  <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ocean-900 mb-6">Why Miami for Water Activities?</h2>
    <div class="prose-custom">
      <p>Miami offers the most diverse water activity portfolio of any US city. With 28.2 million annual visitors and $1.5 billion in entertainment spend, the demand is massive, but the content gap is wide open.</p>
      <p>Here's what makes Miami special:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Biscayne National Park</strong>, 95% underwater, with living coral reefs just 30 minutes from downtown</li>
        <li><strong>South Beach jet ski</strong>, iconic Art Deco backdrop for high-speed water adventures</li>
        <li><strong>Mangrove kayaking</strong>, Oleta River State Park offers Florida's urban wilderness experience</li>
        <li><strong>Efoil</strong>, Miami is one of the first US cities with efoil operators (RideFoil Miami, eFoil Miami)</li>
        <li><strong>Celebrity homes boat tours</strong>, Star Island and Millionaires Row are world-famous routes</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Whether you're a first-time snorkeler or an experienced water sports enthusiast, Miami has something for every skill level.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Best time to visit -->
  <section class="bg-sand-50 py-12">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ocean-900 mb-6">Best Time for Water Activities in Miami</h2>
      <div class="prose-custom">
        <p>Miami's water activity season runs year-round, but the sweet spot is <strong>March through June</strong>, warm water, calm seas, and fewer crowds than peak summer.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Best overall:</strong> March–June (warm, calm, manageable crowds)</li>
          <li><strong>Peak season:</strong> July–August (hottest, busiest, but perfect water temps)</li>
          <li><strong>Shoulder season:</strong> September–November (hurricane risk, but great deals)</li>
          <li><strong>Winter:</strong> December–February (cooler air, but water stays swimmable at 72–76°F)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>